      ":question/id": "89998dc2-c3dd-50ed-be72-12d10d80fa74",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix with $4$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=8$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=6$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{10} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=10=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false.  Since $A$ has $4$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=10.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 10,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have that $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =10 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =10-4 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" III only.\"",
